  "prefLabel": "Pda 301.05 Emergency",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Pda 301.05 “Emergency” means a situation that requires immediate action to protect the health and safety of individuals or to prevent damage to property or the environment, including, but not limited to:\n\n(a) Severe weather conditions; or\n\n(b) Deteriorating conditions on board a vessel that jeopardize its seaworthiness or the ability of the master of the vessel to control the vessel.\n\nSource. #7870, eff 4-12-03; ss by #9891-A, eff 4-1-11; ss by #12760, eff 4-19-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/pda100-700.html"
